    "title": "Gallery AI last-seen memory at normal speed",
    "description": "A stationary brown tank loses sight of the player behind a wall, holds its turret on the last position it actually observed for AI_LAST_SEEN_TICKS, then hands off to the idle search sweep. Issue #372's artefact. Shot from the TOP view, not the game camera: the whole content of the clip is where a turret points relative to a target it cannot see, and the game camera's oblique angle foreshortens exactly that bearing. The clip is evidence for a judgement -- whether this reads as attentive rather than omniscient -- not a measurement; the measurable parts are pinned in tools/gallery/moments.test.ts.",
    "altText": "Top-down view: a brown tank's turret follows a blue tank until the blue tank passes behind a grey wall, then stays pointed at the spot where it disappeared while the blue tank drives back and forth elsewhere, and finally begins sweeping.",
